<title>USA: Uzbek 96/97 grain production flat - U.S. ag attache.</title>
<headline>Uzbek 96/97 grain production flat - U.S. ag attache.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1996-09-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>A U.S. agricultural attache predicted Uzbekistan's 1996/97 grain crop would be the same as the prior year despite efforts to increase production.</p>
<p>&quot;Although final government figures are not yet available, most sources estimate that MY 1996/97 production (excluding rice) will be about the same as the 2.7 MMT (million metric tonnes) produced in MY 1995/96,&quot; the attache wrote.</p>
<p>He said though wheat area increased, yields continued to decline. Uzbekistan had set a 4.8 million tonne output target.</p>
<p>The attache said Kazakhstan is expected to provide the bulk of Uzbekistan's MY 1996/97 import requirements.</p>
</text>
